# Allow-list: `dof adopt` imports only these paths from ~/.config/ghostty.
#
# The directory holds more state and third-party material than config, so an
# allow-list is shorter than the ignore-list would be.

config
toggle-shader.sh
shaders/cursor_tail.glsl
shaders/LICENSE

# ── Deliberately NOT listed ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# shader.conf        The on/off fragment toggle-shader.sh rewrites on every
#                    keypress. It is state, not config. Under link mode each
#                    toggle would dirty `git status`, which is exactly the
#                    trustedWorkspaces mistake from the agy adoption. The main
#                    config includes it with `?` so its absence is fine, and
#                    the toggle script creates it on first use.
#
# shaders/.git/      shaders/ is a shallow clone of sahaj-b/ghostty-cursor-shaders
# shaders/.gitignore (MIT). Its .git internals are not ours to version, and a
# shaders/README.md  nested .gitignore would alter this repo's ignore rules for
#                    the subtree. Once cursor_tail.glsl is link-managed from
#                    here, that clone is vestigial anyway.
#
# shaders/*.glsl     The other seven shaders are upstream verbatim, unmodified.
#  (except tail)     Same call as the kitty themes: do not vendor third-party
#                    files we have not touched; record where they come from.
#                    cursor_tail.glsl is different because THRESHOLD_MIN_DISTANCE
#                    was changed (1.5 → 2.0, see notes/ghostty.md), which makes
#                    it ours to keep. LICENSE rides along because MIT asks for it.
#                    To try another shader: git clone the upstream repo.
#
# *.dof-bak-*        dof's own backups, already excluded by the built-in list.
